Slice 079b (R-T30, R-SO10, Q3 of slice 079): the selected compiler of a tool command is also the `roc` on `PATH` when ranks 2 (`ROC_TOOLCHAIN`) and 6 (`default-roc`) give nothing and its id is a nightly or a release (rank 7). It is looked up only then, so each run with no default and no `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` that chooses a compiler has the call `path_roc` (and the calls of slice 022b the first time) before the choice.  Slice 080 (R-SO24, R-SO6): with no `default-roc` the newest installed nightly or release is rank 6, so one `list_dirs` of `<cache>/toolchains` comes first (`ToolFlow.selected_for!`), and the `path_roc` lookup (rank 7) only when nothing is installed.
